1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,872
Monday, ten in the morning.

2
00:00:01,922 --> 00:00:07,128
Aziz sits in a café, on the café Wi-Fi, and logs in to the mobile bank.

3
00:00:07,178 --> 00:00:09,672
He types the code from the SMS.

4
00:00:09,722 --> 00:00:16,304
It is the right code, and still the app says: We cannot complete this now.

5
00:00:16,354 --> 00:00:18,728
Why would a platform refuse a correct code?

6
00:00:18,778 --> 00:00:25,208
In Lesson 11, the counters guarded the code itself: its life, its tries, its requests.

7
00:00:25,258 --> 00:00:28,448
This lesson adds the check that no counter can do.

8
00:00:28,498 --> 00:00:30,752
TAF looks at where the code arrived.

9
00:00:30,802 --> 00:00:32,864
And it does this only in the master app.

10
00:00:32,914 --> 00:00:35,120
First, what TAF is.

11
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:40,472
It is a state service of the mobile operators, and its agent already runs in the bank's network.

12
00:00:40,522 --> 00:00:45,824
In the master app, TAF sends every code for a registration and a login.

13
00:00:45,874 --> 00:00:50,888
Its part inside the app checks that the SMS arrived on this phone, with this SIM card.

14
00:00:50,938 --> 00:00:53,360
Then TAF gives a verdict.

15
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:57,344
I think the most important word in this lesson is recommendation.

16
00:00:57,394 --> 00:00:59,216
The verdict is advice.

17
00:00:59,266 --> 00:01:02,864
The platform makes the decision, with the policy of the bank.

18
00:01:02,914 --> 00:01:04,736
The app has a job too.

19
00:01:04,786 --> 00:01:07,568
It starts the TAF part after an install.

20
00:01:07,618 --> 00:01:10,952
It sends the id of that part with each code request.

21
00:01:11,002 --> 00:01:14,768
It gives each typed code to the TAF part first.

22
00:01:14,818 --> 00:01:18,176
And it tells the TAF part at each logout.

23
00:01:18,226 --> 00:01:22,040
If the app skips a step, the verdict simply comes back negative.

24
00:01:22,090 --> 00:01:26,624
After a correct code, the platform asks TAF for two verdicts.

25
00:01:26,674 --> 00:01:40,592
The basic verdict is seven plain answers: the account is active, the code is usable, the SMS was sent, the status is valid, the code was verified, the device and the SIM card match, and the phone is not a clone.

26
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:45,752
The risk verdict is a colour: Green, Yellow or Red, with a main reason.

27
00:01:45,802 --> 00:01:52,664
The risk verdict can take a moment, so the platform asks again at a set interval, until the configured waiting time ends.

28
00:01:52,714 --> 00:01:56,096
If it is still not ready, the basic verdict decides.

29
00:01:56,146 --> 00:01:58,520
All seven answers true means Green.

30
00:01:58,570 --> 00:02:00,392
One false answer means Red.

31
00:02:00,442 --> 00:02:02,264
Back to the café.

32
00:02:02,314 --> 00:02:04,712
The risk verdict did not arrive in time.

33
00:02:04,762 --> 00:02:10,784
On the café Wi-Fi, the device and the SIM card did not match, so the basic verdict said Red.

34
00:02:10,834 --> 00:02:12,656
Red means refuse.

35
00:02:12,706 --> 00:02:14,408
The login attempt ends.

36
00:02:14,458 --> 00:02:18,056
But a refusal blocks nothing, and it changes no counter.

37
00:02:18,106 --> 00:02:23,528
The app shows one piece of advice: use the mobile network of your operator, not Wi-Fi.

38
00:02:23,578 --> 00:02:26,456
Aziz switches off the Wi-Fi and tries again.

39
00:02:26,506 --> 00:02:28,400
This time the verdict is Green.

40
00:02:28,450 --> 00:02:34,952
The login continues, and his session in the master app gets the stronger rank, which Lesson 29 explains.

41
00:02:35,002 --> 00:02:37,160
Yellow is the careful colour.

42
00:02:37,210 --> 00:02:44,720
For a customer who was ever at level two, Yellow means: show the consent screen, and then a MyID re-check on this device.

43
00:02:44,770 --> 00:02:50,144
If his face passes, the device becomes trusted and the session gets the stronger rank.

44
00:02:50,194 --> 00:02:52,952
If it fails, the platform refuses.

45
00:02:53,002 --> 00:03:02,552
For anyone else, and that includes every new registration, Yellow means refuse, with the reason text of TAF, in the language of the journey.

46
00:03:02,602 --> 00:03:04,832
There is no MyID to fall back on yet.

47
00:03:04,882 --> 00:03:06,704
Now fast forward.

48
00:03:06,754 --> 00:03:10,832
Aziz is at level two, and he logs in with a Green verdict.

49
00:03:10,882 --> 00:03:14,816
The app asks for one more thing: the face biometric of his own phone.

50
00:03:14,866 --> 00:03:17,744
This is not MyID, and it gives no level.

51
00:03:17,794 --> 00:03:25,304
When it succeeds, the platform sends a face confirmation to TAF, with his personal identification number and his phone number.

52
00:03:25,354 --> 00:03:31,160
The platform sends it, never the app, so the personal identification number never reaches the phone.

53
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:37,928
If TAF fails to answer, the login still continues, and the confirmation waits for the next login.

54
00:03:37,978 --> 00:03:41,696
For a customer at level one, there is no face confirmation at all.

55
00:03:41,746 --> 00:03:43,664
What if TAF is down?

56
00:03:43,714 --> 00:03:48,344
The platform checks its health at a set interval, and each call has a timeout.

57
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:53,384
When TAF does not answer, the bank's SMS service sends the code.

58
00:03:53,434 --> 00:03:55,520
The attempt is marked not scored.

59
00:03:55,570 --> 00:03:59,624
There is no verdict, no face confirmation and no ownership check.

60
00:03:59,674 --> 00:04:05,744
The platform writes an audit event, tells the bank's antifraud system, and alerts operations.

61
00:04:05,794 --> 00:04:09,776
The session keeps the weaker rank, until a later Green raises it.

62
00:04:09,826 --> 00:04:14,312
When TAF is back, the next code goes through TAF again.

63
00:04:14,362 --> 00:04:17,600
And one case where the platform must not fall back.

64
00:04:17,650 --> 00:04:21,968
On the state services portal, a person can choose one trusted bank.

65
00:04:22,018 --> 00:04:26,960
If Aziz once chose a different bank, TAF refuses to send the code.

66
00:04:27,010 --> 00:04:28,328
That is not an outage.

67
00:04:28,378 --> 00:04:32,624
The platform stops, and it sends no code through any other channel.

68
00:04:32,674 --> 00:04:36,920
The app tells Aziz to change the setting there, or to contact the bank.

69
00:04:36,970 --> 00:04:39,872
Last, what TAF receives.

70
00:04:39,922 --> 00:04:46,304
The phone number, a request id, the code, the type of message, the device model and the language.

71
00:04:46,354 --> 00:04:53,000
The personal identification number goes only for the face confirmation, and for the phone ownership check in Lesson 18.

72
00:04:53,050 --> 00:04:57,032
Never a name, a document, an address or a photo.

73
00:04:57,082 --> 00:04:58,904
To recap.

74
00:04:58,954 --> 00:05:03,248
In the master app, TAF sends the code and gives a verdict.

75
00:05:03,298 --> 00:05:10,256
The platform decides: Green continues, Yellow asks for MyID or refuses, Red refuses.

76
00:05:10,306 --> 00:05:14,504
When TAF is down, the code still comes, but not scored.

77
00:05:14,554 --> 00:05:17,600
When the customer chose another bank, nothing comes.

78
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:21,776
But every one of these logins began before any code, with a password.

79
00:05:21,826 --> 00:05:26,072
How does the platform keep a password that it must check, but can never read?

80
00:05:26,122 --> 00:05:27,944
Next: the password.
